---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import {
  BUSINESS_NAME,
  OWNER_NAME,
  PHONE_DISPLAY,
  PHONE_E164,
  EMAIL,
  LOCALITY,
} from '../data/business';

const title = "Privacy Policy | ROH Tiling Wellington";
const description = "How ROH Tiling collects, uses and protects your personal information under the New Zealand Privacy Act 2020.";
const canonical = "/privacy";
const breadcrumbs = [{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Privacy Policy" }];

const updated = "12 August 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <PageHeader
    title="Privacy Policy"
    subtitle="What we collect, why we collect it, and what we do with it."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container legal">
      <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p class="legal__lead">
        {BUSINESS_NAME} ({OWNER_NAME}) operates <strong>rohtiling.co.nz</strong>. We handle personal
        information in accordance with the New Zealand <strong>Privacy Act 2020</strong>. This policy
        explains what we collect and what we do with it. It is short because we collect very little.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
      <p>Only what you give us, and only when you choose to contact us:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your name</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Phone number and email address</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Suburb or job location</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Details of the work you are enquiring about</strong>, including anything you tell us about your property</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We collect this when you submit the form on our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, call us,
        email us, message us on social media, or when we visit your property to quote.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> run analytics, advertising or tracking scripts on this website, and we
        do not set our own cookies. We do not collect payment card details through this website.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Why we collect it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your enquiry and prepare a quote</li>
        <li>To arrange access, schedule work and carry out the job</li>
        <li>To invoice you and keep records required by New Zealand tax law</li>
        <li>To deal with any warranty or defect claim afterwards</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We will not add you to a marketing list or send you promotional email unless you have asked us to.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell or trade your information. We share it only where it is necessary to do the job or
        run the business:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Suppliers and other trades</strong> — for example a plumber or electrician working on the same job, or a tile supplier arranging delivery to your address</li>
        <li><strong>Our email and hosting providers</strong> — enquiries submitted through the contact form are transmitted by our email delivery provider and stored in our email account</li>
        <li><strong>Our accountant and the Inland Revenue Department</strong> — for invoicing and tax records</li>
        <li><strong>Where the law requires it</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Third-party services on this website</h2>
      <p>
        Two third-party services load when you view this site. Both are provided by Google, and both
        receive your IP address and browser information as a normal part of serving content:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — supplies the typefaces used across the site</li>
        <li><strong>Google Maps</strong> — the service-area map embedded on the contact page. This loads only on that page, and Google may set its own cookies through it</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Their handling of that data is governed by Google's own privacy policy, not ours. Our website also
        links to our Google Business Profile and Instagram; once you follow those links you are on their
        platforms and their privacy policies apply.
      </p>

      <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries that do not lead to work are kept for up to <strong>2 years</strong>. Records relating to
        completed jobs — quotes, invoices and job notes — are kept for at least <strong>7 years</strong>, as
        required for tax purposes, and because they may be needed if a workmanship question arises later.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Storage and security</h2>
      <p>
        Your information is held in our email account and business records, protected by passwords and
        two-factor authentication where available. Some of these services store data on servers outside New
        Zealand. No system is perfectly secure, but we take reasonable steps to protect your information
        against loss, misuse and unauthorised access.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the Privacy Act 2020 you have the right to <strong>ask what personal information we hold about
        you</strong>, and to <strong>ask us to correct it</strong> if it is wrong. Email
        <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> or call <a href={`tel:${PHONE_E164}`}>{PHONE_DISPLAY}</a> and we
        will respond within 20 working days, as the Act requires.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are not satisfied with how we have handled your information, you can complain to the Office of
        the Privacy Commissioner at <a href="https://www.privacy.org.nz" rel="noopener" target="_blank">privacy.org.nz</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Children</h2>
      <p>
        This website and our services are directed at property owners and trade clients. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change how we handle personal information we will update this page and the date at the top.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <address class="legal__contact">
        <strong>{BUSINESS_NAME}</strong><br />
        {LOCALITY}<br />
        <a href={`tel:${PHONE_E164}`}>{PHONE_DISPLAY}</a><br />
        <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>
      </address>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
